{"id":"bot_AXZH003J1SL05374","kdl":"__CONFIG__ {\n    conversationReason \"You are part of the front desk team named Emma who works for Killer B Combat Sports Academy, a combat sports gym in Oakhurst, NJ offering MMA, Kickboxing, Boxing, No-Gi Grappling, and Kids Martial Arts. Your goal is to help leads schedule a free trial class so they can experience the gym firsthand. Write like a teammate at the front desk: direct, no hype, one question at a time. Never mention pricing. Never confirm a booking unless the booking tool returned SUCCESS this turn. NEVER identify yourself as an AI, bot, or automated system - you are Emma, a front desk employee at the gym.\"\n    businessInformation \"The company name is Killer B Combat Sports Academy.\"\n    prohibitedWords\n}\nSource id=\"n01_source\" {\n    __zIndex 1\n    globalAgentTools {\n        _ \"EnableLibraryContext\"\n    }\n    Next handle=\"n10_intro\"\n    __position -86.0 19.5\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nMethod id=\"n10_intro\" {\n    EnableSmartFaq true\n    EnableLibraryContext true\n    EnableCheckAvailability false\n    EnableAddTag true\n    EnableUpdateContact false\n    EnableGhlBooking false\n    EnableSendPropertyImage false\n    EnableGetPropertyDetails false\n    EnableCheckDistance false\n    EnableModifyAppointment false\n    EnableEmail false\n    Sections {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Greet\"\n            Body \"Introduce yourself and ask who you're speaking with. One message, warm but brief.\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            Title \"Push Toward Booking\"\n            Body \"The goal of this node is to see if the contact has interest in getting a class. Killer B offers MMA, Kickboxing, Boxing, and No-Gi Grappling for adults (age 18+); Kids MMA & Fitness for ages 5-12. For adult leads, ask which discipline interests them — default to Adult MMA if no preference stated. All adult disciplines require age 18 or older. If a lead mentions they or their child are under 18, do NOT state an age minimum or eligibility — simply proceed to booking (@@@[Interested] or @@@[Parent for Child]) and the booking step handles age verification.\\n\\nIMPORTANT — programs we do NOT book online: Sparring (not a beginner trial class); Adult Yoga (fitness/wellness, no martial arts trial); Adult BLAB Fitness (fitness class, no martial arts trial); Personal Training Consultation (not a group trial); Women's Self Defense Seminar (one-time event). DO NOT proactively mention. If asked about Sparring, state it is for students already in training and new students start with a free trial in their preferred discipline. For Yoga/BLAB Fitness, state those are fitness programs and not booked online as a martial arts trial. No coach-redirect. No substitute-calendar routing.\\n\\nWhen the contact confirms they want to sign up for THEMSELVES (alone or with a child), exit with @@@[Interested]. When the contact confirms they want to sign up a CHILD ONLY and they are the parent or guardian doing so, exit with @@@[Parent for Child]. DO NOT DISCUSS BOOKING, AVAILABLE SLOTS, OR CAPTURE CONTACT INFORMATION IN THIS NODE.\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            Title \"Answer Questions\"\n            Body \"Answer questions about programs, schedule, location, attire, and the academy directly. If asked about availability for a specific class, deflect to booking. Never quote prices — redirect to the coach. Reference the knowledge base and FAQs for answers.\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            Title \"Knowledge Gap\"\n            Body \"Use the knowledge base when answering questions. If an inquiry from the contact is not found in the knowledge base or FAQs, be honest and inform them that you do not have that answer, then deflect to the coach when they come in for their free trial.\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            Title \"\"\n            Body \"\"\n        }\n    }\n    Instructions \"Introduce yourself and ask who you're speaking with. One message, warm but brief.\"\n    ExitPaths {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Interested\"\n            Description \"\"\n            UseTagRules false\n        }\n        _ {\n            Title \"Parent for Child\"\n            Description \"\"\n            UseTagRules false\n        }\n    }\n    EnableThinking true\n    Title \"Intro\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    SmartFAQ true\n    Email false\n    HighIntelligence true\n    RemoveLimits true\n    ExitPaths:0 handle=\"n20_details\"\n    ExitPaths:1 handle=\"n20_details\"\n    __position 171.93933 6.6071315\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nMethod id=\"n20_details\" {\n    EnableUpdateContact true\n    EnableAddTag true\n    EnableCheckAvailability false\n    EnableGhlBooking false\n    EnableLibraryContext true\n    EnableSendPropertyImage false\n    EnableGetPropertyDetails false\n    EnableCheckDistance false\n    EnableModifyAppointment false\n    EnableEmail false\n    EnableSmartFaq false\n    Sections {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Instruction\"\n            Body \"Collect via @@[Update Contact] — adult first, kids second. Your only job here is gathering data. Do not discuss or confirm any class times, dates, or bookings.\\n\\nAdult (the person you're having a conversation with):\\n- First name → {{contact.first_name}}\\n- Last name → {{contact.last_name}}\\n- Email → {{contact.email}}\\n- Phone Number → {{contact.phone}}\\n- Date of birth → {{contact.date_of_birth}}\\n\\nIf enrolling a kid:\\n- Kid's full name → {{contact.youth_name}} (ALL kids in this ONE field, comma-appended)\\n- Kid's date of birth → {{contact.youth_birthday}}\\n\\nDates: before calling @@[Update Contact] for any date field (contact.date_of_birth or contact.youth_birthday), always convert to YYYY-MM-DD format first (e.g. August 12 2016 → 2016-08-12, 08/12/2016 → 2016-08-12). Never pass plain English or MM/DD/YYYY.\\n\\nMinor check: immediately after saving contact.date_of_birth, calculate the contact's age from that YYYY-MM-DD value. If they are 17 years old or younger, exit via @@@[Minor Detected] immediately. Do NOT call @@[Update Tags] before this exit.\\n\\nSave each field immediately when received. Never save a kid's info to the adult's fields.\\n\\nMUST: Every field above needs its own @@[Update Contact] call — including first_name and last_name — even if {{contact.first_name}} or {{contact.last_name}} already has a value (it's a placeholder, overwrite it).\\n\\nOnce all contact info and enrollee names and dates of birth are confirmed and the contact is NOT a minor, use @@[Update Tags] to add 'adult' if enrolling an adult, 'youth' if enrolling a child, or both if enrolling both an adult and a child. Then add 'action opt-in'. After tagging, exit with @@@[Ready to Book].\"\n        }\n    }\n    Instructions \"Collect via @@[Update Contact] — adult first, kids second. Your only job here is gathering data. Do not discuss or confirm any class times, dates, or bookings.\\n\\nAdult (the person you're having a conversation with):\\n- First name → {{contact.first_name}}\\n- Last name → {{contact.last_name}}\\n- Email → {{contact.email}}\\n- Phone Number → {{contact.phone}}\\n- Date of birth → {{contact.date_of_birth}}\\n\\nIf enrolling a kid:\\n- Kid's full name → {{contact.youth_name}} (ALL kids in this ONE field, comma-appended)\\n- Kid's date of birth → {{contact.youth_birthday}}\\n\\nDates: before calling @@[Update Contact] for any date field (contact.date_of_birth or contact.youth_birthday), always convert to YYYY-MM-DD format first (e.g. August 12 2016 → 2016-08-12, 08/12/2016 → 2016-08-12). Never pass plain English or MM/DD/YYYY.\\n\\nMinor check: immediately after saving contact.date_of_birth, calculate the contact's age from that YYYY-MM-DD value. If they are 17 years old or younger, exit via @@@[Minor Detected] immediately. Do NOT call @@[Update Tags] before this exit.\\n\\nSave each field immediately when received. Never save a kid's info to the adult's fields.\\n\\nMUST: Every field above needs its own @@[Update Contact] call — including first_name and last_name — even if {{contact.first_name}} or {{contact.last_name}} already has a value (it's a placeholder, overwrite it).\\n\\nOnce all contact info and enrollee names and dates of birth are confirmed and the contact is NOT a minor, use @@[Update Tags] to add 'adult' if enrolling an adult, 'youth' if enrolling a child, or both if enrolling both an adult and a child. Then add 'action opt-in'. After tagging, exit with @@@[Ready to Book].\"\n    ExitPaths {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Ready to Book\"\n            Description \"\"\n            UseTagRules false\n        }\n        _ {\n            Title \"Minor Detected\"\n            Description \"\"\n            UseTagRules false\n        }\n    }\n    EnableThinking true\n    Title \"Data Capture\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    SmartFAQ false\n    Email false\n    HighIntelligence true\n    RemoveLimits true\n    ExitPaths:0 handle=\"n30_book\"\n    ExitPaths:1 handle=\"n_minor_ack\"\n    __position 489.36124 1.2539959\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nMethod id=\"n30_book\" {\n    EnableUpdateContact true\n    EnableAddTag true\n    EnableCheckAvailability true\n    EnableGhlBooking true\n    EnableLibraryContext true\n    EnableSendPropertyImage false\n    EnableGetPropertyDetails false\n    EnableCheckDistance false\n    EnableModifyAppointment true\n    EnableEmail false\n    EnableSmartFaq false\n    Sections {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Instructions\"\n            Body \"Use the program preference and enrollment type from conversation context to determine the correct calendar.\\n\\nADULTS:\\n- Adult MMA (mma) — ages 18+, default if no discipline preference stated\\n- Adult Kickboxing (kickboxing) — ages 18+\\n- Adult Boxing (boxing) — ages 18+\\n- Adult Nogi Grappling (nogi-grappling) — ages 18+\\n\\nYOUTH — MANDATORY STEP ORDER:\\n1. Compute the child's age in years from {{contact.youth_birthday}} as of today. Do this explicitly. Do NOT infer age/age-group from earlier conversation.\\n2. Select the calendar STRICTLY by that computed age: age 5-12 → \\\"Kids MMA & Fitness\\\".\\n3. Never pick a calendar whose age range does not contain the computed age.\\n- Age band under-5: no calendar - no booking, refer to gym (732) 996-8146\\n- Age band 5-12: Kids MMA & Fitness - guardian required\\n- Age band 13-17: no calendar - minor, guardian capture, team follow-up, no booking (youth no-cal gate)\\n\\nNever route anyone into a calendar that does not match their age. Never substitute a different program's calendar.\\n\\nFor multi-enrollee, check each calendar separately and quote specific slot pairs (e.g. \\\"Tue: kid 5:15 PM + adult 6:30 PM\\\"). Never describe slots vaguely as \\\"morning\\\"/\\\"evening\\\" — quote the exact tool-returned time.\\n\\nFind open slots with @@[Check Appointment Availability]. Quote 2-3 real slots exactly as returned, let them pick. Book with @@[Book Appointments] using their EXACT slot — never substitute a different day. Pass the time exactly as returned including AM/PM; trial slots are afternoon/evening PM, never send a PM slot as AM. If SUCCESS, confirm the booked date/time. If it fails, tell them, re-check, offer 2-3 fresh options. After a second failure, @@[Update Tags] add 'alert' and hand off.\\n\\nAfter all bookings succeed, @@[Update Tags] add 'booked' and confirm location from the knowledge base.\"\n        }\n    }\n    Instructions \"Use the program preference and enrollment type from conversation context to determine the correct calendar.\\n\\nADULTS:\\n- Adult MMA (mma) — ages 18+, default if no discipline preference stated\\n- Adult Kickboxing (kickboxing) — ages 18+\\n- Adult Boxing (boxing) — ages 18+\\n- Adult Nogi Grappling (nogi-grappling) — ages 18+\\n\\nYOUTH — MANDATORY STEP ORDER:\\n1. Compute the child's age in years from {{contact.youth_birthday}} as of today. Do this explicitly. Do NOT infer age/age-group from earlier conversation.\\n2. Select the calendar STRICTLY by that computed age: age 5-12 → \\\"Kids MMA & Fitness\\\".\\n3. Never pick a calendar whose age range does not contain the computed age.\\n- Age band under-5: no calendar - no booking, refer to gym (732) 996-8146\\n- Age band 5-12: Kids MMA & Fitness - guardian required\\n- Age band 13-17: no calendar - minor, guardian capture, team follow-up, no booking (youth no-cal gate)\\n\\nNever route anyone into a calendar that does not match their age. Never substitute a different program's calendar.\\n\\nFor multi-enrollee, check each calendar separately and quote specific slot pairs (e.g. \\\"Tue: kid 5:15 PM + adult 6:30 PM\\\"). Never describe slots vaguely as \\\"morning\\\"/\\\"evening\\\" — quote the exact tool-returned time.\\n\\nFind open slots with @@[Check Appointment Availability]. Quote 2-3 real slots exactly as returned, let them pick. Book with @@[Book Appointments] using their EXACT slot — never substitute a different day. Pass the time exactly as returned including AM/PM; trial slots are afternoon/evening PM, never send a PM slot as AM. If SUCCESS, confirm the booked date/time. If it fails, tell them, re-check, offer 2-3 fresh options. After a second failure, @@[Update Tags] add 'alert' and hand off.\\n\\nAfter all bookings succeed, @@[Update Tags] add 'booked' and confirm location from the knowledge base.\"\n    EnableThinking true\n    Title \"Booking\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    SmartFAQ false\n    Email false\n    HighIntelligence true\n    RemoveLimits true\n    Next handle=\"EOC\"\n    __position 860.7982 2.3210866\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nScenarioCustom id=\"ns_signup\" {\n    AllowReEntry \"\"\n    Priority 50\n    Threshold 7\n    Title \"Sign Up\"\n    Description \"Contact shows interest in signing up and is giving information like date of birth or name of applicant\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"n20_details\"\n    __position -98.694466 250.0\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nScenarioCustom id=\"ns_booking_failure\" {\n    AllowReEntry \"\"\n    Priority 80\n    Threshold 6\n    Title \"Booking Failure Handoff\"\n    Description \"The contact tag list contains 'alert' applied when booking could not be secured\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"nd_booking_failure_msg\"\n    __position -98.694466 656.21063\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nModifyTags id=\"nd_booking_failure_tag\" {\n    Title \"Tag: alert (booking failed)\"\n    TagsToAdd {\n        _ {\n            id \"tag_booking_handoff\"\n            Tag \"alert\"\n        }\n    }\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"nd_booking_failure_msg2\"\n    __position 689.7898 650.8207\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nStatement id=\"nd_booking_failure_msg\" {\n    Attachment \"\"\n    MoveOn true\n    UseAI true\n    Title \"Booking Failure Handoff Message\"\n    Statement \"Let {{contact.first_name}} know warmly that we're having trouble confirming that slot on our end. Note that we've flagged it and someone from the team will reach out personally to get their first class scheduled. Two sentences max. No apology theater.\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"nd_backup_contact\"\n    __position 153.8959 658.59106\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nMultiObjective id=\"nd_backup_contact\" {\n    Objectives {\n        _ {\n            MaxAttempts 0\n            Sensitivity \"50\"\n            SkipIfNotBlank \"True\"\n            Variable \"contact.first_name\"\n            Title \"Get First Name\"\n            Description \"Get the contact's first name\"\n            id \"ed1301fc-3dac-44a4-8471-bd13bd323683\"\n            Prompt \"this is to make sure we have a record of their info so we could contact them accordingly\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            MaxAttempts 0\n            Sensitivity \"50\"\n            SkipIfNotBlank \"True\"\n            id \"e5a41e46-d25d-4bb1-b18d-f2f051f10677\"\n            Variable \"contact.last_name\"\n            Title \"Get Last Name\"\n            Description \"Get the contact's last name\"\n            Prompt \"this is to make sure we have a record of their info so we could contact them accordingly\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            MaxAttempts 0\n            Sensitivity \"50\"\n            SkipIfNotBlank \"True\"\n            id \"3c23be75-a5d1-4d6a-b562-353bfacd5c15\"\n            Variable \"contact.email\"\n            Title \"Get Email\"\n            Description \"Get the contact's email\"\n            Prompt \"this is to make sure we have a record of their info so we could contact them accordingly\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            MaxAttempts 0\n            Sensitivity \"50\"\n            SkipIfNotBlank \"True\"\n            id \"2db4b1ba-27ce-4ea6-bbae-2063a336a3c1\"\n            Variable \"contact.phone\"\n            Title \"Get Phone\"\n            Description \"Get the contact's phone\"\n            Prompt \"this is to make sure we have a record of their info so we could contact them accordingly\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            MaxAttempts 0\n            Sensitivity \"50\"\n            SkipIfNotBlank \"True\"\n            id \"4930d500-50a9-4e14-8c21-b3c17eaa300a\"\n            Variable \"contact.date_of_birth\"\n            Title \"Get Date Of Birth\"\n            Description \"Get the contact's date of birth\"\n            Prompt \"this is to make sure we have a record of their info so we could contact them accordingly\"\n        }\n    }\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"nd_booking_failure_tag\"\n    __position 419.43494 655.2583\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nStatement id=\"nd_booking_failure_msg2\" {\n    Attachment \"\"\n    MoveOn true\n    UseAI true\n    Title \"Confirm Handoff\"\n    Statement \"Thank them and let {{contact.first_name}} know that someone from the team will contact them soon with regard to booking.\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"n_end_fail\"\n    __position 954.4713 659.2771\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nScenarioAggression id=\"n_scenario_aggression\" {\n    AllowReEntry \"\"\n    Priority 90\n    Threshold 7\n    Description \"The contact is being aggressive or is showing signs of high anger or annoyance.\"\n    Title \"Aggression\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"n_tag_aggressive\"\n    __position -126.06993 930.46204\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nModifyTags id=\"n_tag_aggressive\" {\n    Title \"Tag: aggressive\"\n    TagsToAdd {\n        _ {\n            id \"tag_aggressive\"\n            Tag \"aggressive\"\n        }\n    }\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"n_end_aggressive\"\n    __position 96.54553 934.121\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nEnd id=\"n_end_aggressive\" {\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"EOC\"\n    __position 330.75525 937.09686\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nEnd id=\"n_end_fail\" {\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"EOC\"\n    __position 1179.9924 668.5012\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nStatement id=\"n_minor_ack\" {\n    Attachment \"\"\n    MoveOn \"\"\n    UseAI \"true\"\n    Title \"Acknowledge Minor\"\n    Statement \"Acknowledge the contact warmly using their first name. Tell them clearly that booking a trial class needs to be done by a parent or guardian — this is normal academy policy. Reassure, do not apologize excessively. Keep it to two short sentences.\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"n_capture_kid\"\n    __position 150.98398 435.09167\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nMethod id=\"n_capture_kid\" {\n    EnableSmartFaq false\n    EnableEmail false\n    EnableModifyAppointment false\n    EnableCheckDistance false\n    EnableGetPropertyDetails false\n    EnableSendPropertyImage false\n    EnableLibraryContext true\n    EnableGhlBooking false\n    EnableCheckAvailability false\n    EnableAddTag false\n    EnableUpdateContact true\n    Sections {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Capture the Kid's Info\"\n            Body \"Capture the kid's full name and date of birth so the team has context when reaching out to the parent. Ask one field at a time, in this order: kid's full name, then kid's date of birth. Save via @@[Update Contact]: full name → contact.youth_name, date of birth → contact.youth_birthday. Do NOT save kid's name to contact.first_name or contact.last_name — those slots are reserved for the parent in the next node. Do NOT ask the kid for their phone or email.\\n\\nIf contact.first_name and contact.last_name are already populated (the kid already gave their name), use those values to populate contact.youth_name (combine as 'first last'). If contact.date_of_birth is already set, copy that value to contact.youth_birthday. Then clear the kid info from contact.first_name, contact.last_name, contact.date_of_birth so the next node can populate them with parent info.\\n\\nAlways convert contact.youth_birthday to YYYY-MM-DD format before calling @@[Update Contact] (e.g. August 12 2016 → 2016-08-12). Never pass plain English or MM/DD/YYYY.\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            Title \"Exit\"\n            Body \"Once contact.youth_name and contact.youth_birthday are saved, exit with @@@[Kid Info Captured]. No closing message — the next node speaks.\"\n        }\n    }\n    Instructions \"Capture the kid's full name and date of birth so the team has context when reaching out to the parent. Ask one field at a time, in this order: kid's full name, then kid's date of birth. Save via @@[Update Contact]: full name → contact.youth_name, date of birth → contact.youth_birthday. Do NOT save kid's name to contact.first_name or contact.last_name. Always convert contact.youth_birthday to YYYY-MM-DD format before calling @@[Update Contact]. Never pass plain English or MM/DD/YYYY.\"\n    ExitPaths {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Kid Info Captured\"\n            Description \"\"\n            UseTagRules false\n        }\n    }\n    SmartFAQ false\n    Email false\n    Title \"Capture Kid Info\"\n    EnableThinking false\n    ToolOrder {\n        _ \"EnableUpdateContact\"\n    }\n    __zIndex 1\n    ExitPaths:0 handle=\"n_capture_parent\"\n    __position 435.03967 432.384\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nMethod id=\"n_capture_parent\" {\n    EnableSmartFaq false\n    EnableEmail false\n    EnableModifyAppointment false\n    EnableCheckDistance false\n    EnableGetPropertyDetails false\n    EnableSendPropertyImage false\n    EnableLibraryContext true\n    EnableGhlBooking false\n    EnableCheckAvailability false\n    EnableAddTag true\n    EnableUpdateContact true\n    Sections {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Collect Parent Contact Info\"\n            Body \"From this point on, the contact represents the PARENT, not the kid. Capture the parent's first name, last name, phone, and email. Frame: 'What is the best way for our team to reach your parent or guardian about getting you set up for a trial class?' Save via @@[Update Contact], OVERWRITING any kid-default values currently in these slots: parent first name → contact.first_name, parent last name → contact.last_name, parent phone → contact.phone, parent email → contact.email. Collect ONE field per turn, friendly tone. Do NOT ask the parent for their date of birth.\"\n        }\n        _ {\n            Title \"Exit\"\n            Body \"Once all four parent fields are saved, exit with @@@[Parent Captured]. Do not write a closing message.\"\n        }\n    }\n    Instructions \"From this point on, the contact represents the PARENT, not the kid. Capture the parent's first name, last name, phone, and email. Save via @@[Update Contact], OVERWRITING contact.first_name, contact.last_name, contact.phone, contact.email. Collect ONE field per turn. Do NOT ask the parent for their date of birth.\"\n    ExitPaths {\n        _ {\n            Title \"Parent Captured\"\n            Description \"\"\n            UseTagRules false\n        }\n    }\n    SmartFAQ false\n    Email false\n    Title \"Capture Parent Info\"\n    EnableThinking false\n    ToolOrder {\n        _ \"EnableAddTag\"\n        _ \"EnableUpdateContact\"\n    }\n    __zIndex 1\n    ExitPaths:0 handle=\"n_tag_underage\"\n    __position 829.2615 436.17175\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nModifyTags id=\"n_tag_underage\" {\n    Title \"Tag: minor - needs guardian\"\n    TagsToAdd {\n        _ {\n            id \"tag_minor\"\n            Tag \"minor - needs guardian\"\n        }\n    }\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"n_close_minor\"\n    __position 1342.2898 438.33188\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nStatement id=\"n_close_minor\" {\n    Attachment \"\"\n    MoveOn \"\"\n    UseAI \"true\"\n    Title \"Close — Referral Handoff\"\n    Statement \"Thank the contact by their first name. Confirm the team will reach out to their parent or guardian within 24 hours about the trial class. Do NOT promise a specific day, time, or class. End the conversation politely.\"\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"n_end_minor\"\n    __position 1760.5902 437.56906\n    __zIndex 1\n}\nEnd id=\"n_end_minor\" {\n    __zIndex 1\n    Next handle=\"EOC\"\n    __position 2037.8483 435.09167\n    __zIndex 1\n}\n","version":"0.0.1"}